From: Lovelace's Square <noreply@lovelacesquare.org>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 10:20:19 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 2/4] Control port `auto`: listen on a free port and name the
 key file after it

`--control auto` (or DECKCRAFT_CONTROL_PORT=auto; `0` means the same)
binds 127.0.0.1:0, so the system picks a free port, and the key file is
written for the port actually bound (control-key.local-<port>). Any
number of windows can then be started with a control channel without
choosing ports, and a client finds each window, and its port, by listing
the key files. As in WordCraft.

- deckcraft: control_server::parse_port (a port number or `auto`, any
  case) for --control and DECKCRAFT_CONTROL_PORT; start() reads the bound
  port back from the listener for the key file and the log.
- docs: control-protocol.md describes `auto` and the key file name.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Esdp3ZTPsHBV41yHxMJHnJ
